# Environment files. Real values live in Vercel; only the placeholder file is
# committed. `*.local` above already covers .env.development.local, and the
# exception has to come last so `vercel link` adding a broad rule cannot quietly
# start ignoring the template.
.env
.env*
!.env.example

# A copy of real values gathered for pasting into the Vercel dashboard. Never
# committed: it is a working file, not a template, and .env* above does not
# match it.
